                    },
                    "message": "if it is IOEXP, why not use the gpioset command?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/clemente/power-cmd",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please document the reason why this can't be done using gpioset if there is a reason, otherwise, please make the change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/clemente/power-cmd",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "```\n# To clearly identify which I2C device the command is sent to, \n# i2ctransfer is used to replace the gpioset command.\n```\n\nThis is the rationale?  I strongly disagree with this.  A gpioset to a named line in the device tree is far clearer.  This random i2ctransfer that I have to decode is not clear at all."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/clemente/power-cmd",
                    "line": 107,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alex-TS-Wang",
                        "email": "alex.ts.wang@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "Alex-TS-Wang"
                    },
                    "message": "I understand your concern. I have changed it to control the GPIO commands on the IO expander, \nas clear and intuitive commands are indeed important for long-term maintenance."
                }
