                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Do we need to wait a certain amount of time and then reset these GPIOs?  How do they go back to 0s?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/clemente/power-cmd",
                    "line": 109,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kimi Chen",
                        "email": "kimi.zy.chen@fii-foxconn.com",
                        "username": "zuyan-kimi"
                    },
                    "message": "After my verification:\nHMC_PGOOD-O and BMC_STBY_CYCLE-O will automatically return to their initial states after AC power cycle.\n\nActually, HMC_PGOOD-O initial state is already \"1\" (it is set in the plat-svc recipe standby-power-enable script).\n\nHowever, I believe that waiting 100ms to ensure the HMC_PGOOD-O hardware state can stabilize and be properly reflected would be more robust."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/state/phosphor-state-manager/clemente/power-cmd",
                    "line": 109,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It wasn\u2019t clear to me that this is effectively triggering a \u201csled cycle\u201d and not an \u201cac cycle\u201d.  I will merge this for now and set something up with our EE to discuss. This is not, in my option, an appropriate design for production."
                }
            ],
